The review has been written to `docs/reviews/fleet-python/fleet-python-05-python-dead-code-cleanup.md`.

**Summary**: Two low-severity findings. Both `obs_to_numpy` and `record_batch_arc_to_polars_df` are trivial wrappers with no callers. The existing API paths work correctly without them — observations are returned as Python lists (via PyO3's automatic `Vec<f64>` conversion) and Arrow batches are converted directly from `RecordBatch` references. Neither represents incomplete feature wiring; they are speculative forward-compatibility wrappers that should be removed.
